<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ventel yr shr dives to loss, plans recovery.</title>
<headline>Ventel yr shr dives to loss, plans recovery.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     3.58 loss   vs 4.21 profit</p>
<p>    Profit for period     1.81 loss   vs 2.12 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.56 loss   vs 2.66 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 none	  vs 0.07</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.39	  vs 0.66</p>
<p>Turnover</p>
<p>    - ongoing operations  40.80	 vs 41.88</p>
<p>Full name: Venter Lesiure and Commerical Trailers Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.38 loss   vs 0.46 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors of the group, which manufactures and sells trailers, said that it had entered the heavy duty high speed trailer market which represented large turnover opportunities. It intended to enter the low speed agricultural trailer market too.</p>
<p>Directors said finality was also being reached with certain retrail chaims which could further increase the group's turnover.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
